{
  "name": "Track car deals and price drops in Slack with Auto.dev",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Track a car's market: deal alerts and price drops in Slack\n\n### How it works\nFor anyone shopping for one specific vehicle: a make and model in a year, price and mileage range, near a ZIP code.\n\n- **New listings.** The trigger passes on listings that are new since its last check. Each one is compared with the average price of similar cars and saved to an n8n data table. Cars priced no more than $500 over the average are posted to Slack.\n- **Price drops.** Once a day it compares current prices with the table. A car whose price fell is posted to Slack, and the table is updated.\n\nThe first check only records what is already listed. A Free plan request returns up to 20 listings, so the average and the daily check each cover 20 cars.\n\n### Setup\n1. This template uses the verified community node `n8n-nodes-autodev` (tested with version 0.1.0 on n8n 2.47). It works on n8n Cloud and self-hosted: an owner or admin installs it from the nodes panel ([guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/verified-install/)).\n2. Create an **Auto.dev API** credential with a key from [auto.dev](https://www.auto.dev/dashboard/api-keys). Every call is on the Free plan: one request per check, one more when a listing is new, and one a day for price drops.\n3. Run **Create the market log** once. It adds the `Car market log` data table.\n4. In **Watch for new listings**, set your search and how often to check. The two other Auto.dev nodes read the same search.\n5. In **Send alert to Slack**, add a Slack credential (a bot token with `chat:write`) and pick a channel.\n6. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Customization\nSet -500 to 500 in **Is it fairly priced?** to get only cars $500 under the average. Swap Slack for email or Telegram.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 520
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -160
      ],
      "id": "44e66fd0-05ed-41bf-8019-01aa5dbd607a",
      "name": "Overview"
    },
